WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.610
The UN General Assembly, 10 December 1948.

2
00:00:04.660 --> 00:00:08.510
A vote on the Universal
Declaration of Human Rights.

3
00:00:08.560 --> 00:00:09.770
48 in favour.

4
00:00:09.820 --> 00:00:11.210
8 abstaining.

5
00:00:11.260 --> 00:00:14.950
It is adopted as Resolution 217.

6
00:00:15.000 --> 00:00:19.050
Rights to life, a fair
trial, health and education.

7
00:00:19.100 --> 00:00:22.350
Rights a person holds
simply for being human.

8
00:00:22.400 --> 00:00:25.650
But did that vote bind any of
the countries that cast it?

9
00:00:25.700 --> 00:00:26.990
All 48?

10
00:00:27.040 --> 00:00:28.770
Even the 8 that abstained?

11
00:00:28.820 --> 00:00:32.450
In this mission, you'll pin down who
human rights are claimed against,

12
00:00:32.500 --> 00:00:36.170
and look closely at that 1948 vote.

13
00:00:36.220 --> 00:00:40.210
Then you'll trace what states have
done about human rights since 1948,

14
00:00:40.260 --> 00:00:43.950
up to a UN World Summit in 2005.

15
00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:49.320
Your mission: find out whether the 1948
vote bound the countries that cast it.
